{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"chargeable-combustive-leech","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nIndependent review of ticket 5f4d found two non-blocking hardening gaps in scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py. A file containing invalid UTF-8 is skipped wholesale, and an unallowlisted match prints the complete source line. The current change correctly blocks the target vocabulary, avoids symlink reads, and is approved; this follow-up keeps the additional boundary work scoped separately.\n\n## Plan\n- Define which repository text extensions must fail closed on decode errors while preserving binary-file tolerance.\n- Bound and escape diagnostic excerpts so control characters and very long lines cannot inject or amplify CI logs.\n- Add RED-first behavioral tests for invalid-byte text input, binary controls, control characters, and oversized matching lines.\n- Run make check and the full test suite.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Known text files cannot evade the vocabulary guard by containing an invalid UTF-8 byte.\n- [ ] Binary files remain safely ignored without false positives.\n- [ ] Diagnostics escape control characters and cap source excerpts at a documented maximum length.\n- [ ] Behavioral tests cover all three boundaries and the full suite passes.","id":"8b6c-7583-3e65-4834","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":["vocabulary","security","follow-up"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Harden vocabulary guard decoding and diagnostics"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785275193008510001,"uuid":"d07da293-56bb-465d-b65d-20a3292a60b6"}